# JDBC Test Reviewer

The full reviewer definition is in `.claude/skills/jdbc-test-reviewer/SKILL.md`
(canonical source; also bridged to `.agents/skills/jdbc-test-reviewer` for
Cursor/Codex discovery).

When asked to review JDBC/Java test code under `jdbc/src/test/java/**/*.java`,
read that skill and follow it: review for resource management, test structure,
JDBC call/exception validation, assertions, data retrieval, behavior differences
(`jdbc/BehaviorDifferences.yaml`), code style/DRY, WireMock offline tests, and
coverage gaps; detect flaky-test anti-patterns and map them to rule ids in
`.ai/review/universal-driver-flaky-tests.yaml`; report findings grouped by
High / Medium / Low severity with a coverage table and a checklist.
